Project Design Phase 
The Project Design Phase is the stage where the selected idea is planned and designed in detail before development begins.
Main steps:
Define objectives – Decide what the project should achieve.
Plan the solution – Decide how the project will solve the problem.
Design the structure – Create diagrams, layouts, or models.
Select resources – Identify the required tools, materials, and technologies.
Create a prototype – Develop a basic model of the project.
Review the design – Check whether the design meets the requirements.
